{"type":"message","id":"be201310","parentId":"46d8c2a6","timestamp":"2026-03-31T02:11:30.422Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both sessions_send to aoao timed out. The problem is confirmed - aoao's session is not receiving messages. This is the same issue from the logs.\n\nI need to fix the root cause. The issue is that aoao's session has `deliveryContext.channel = \"webchat\"` but it should be `\"feishu\"`. \n\nLooking at the AGENTS.md:\n- aoao → `agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506`\n\nThe issue is that when aoao was spawned, its session was created with webchat delivery context instead of feishu. \n\nI could try restarting aoao's session, but there's no direct way to do that since sessions_spawn creates new sessions rather than resuming existing ones. The aoao session has a `status: \"done\"` state and a session ID, so I need to figure out if I can actually resume it or if I need to spawn a fresh one. Looking at the actual sessions_list data, aoao doesn't appear in the recent sessions at all—it must have been started much earlier and already completed. Since aoao is unreachable, I'll move forward with what I can handle directly: supporting the two PRs myself using the GitHub skill, and I'll update the project file with the new P1 issues that xixi identified. First, let me check what the GitHub skill can actually do for posting comments.","thinkingSignature":"e786496c96d90c0a1f44e673ada50d112b9a49e8dbc1e6133483831d62b5ca86"},{"type":"text","text":"aoao sessions_send 继续超时。这个问题必须解决才能继续派单。让我检查一下 aoao 的 session 状态，然后直接自己处理可支持的 PR。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_7r786rst86wq_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/github/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":63693,"output":377,"cacheRead":21716,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":85786,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774923073699,"responseId":"061a6042437f8c2caea42aab734b00f6"}}
{"type":"message","id":"ecb45ee7","parentId":"be201310","timestamp":"2026-03-31T02:11:30.483Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_7r786rst86wq_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: github\ndescription: \"Interact with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. Use `gh issue`, `gh pr`, `gh run`, and `gh api` for issues, PRs, CI runs, and advanced queries.\"\n---\n\n# GitHub Skill\n\nUse the `gh` CLI to interact with GitHub. Always specify `--repo owner/repo` when not in a git directory, or use URLs directly.\n\n## Pull Requests\n\nCheck CI status on a PR:\n```bash\ngh pr checks 55 --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nList recent workflow runs:\n```bash\ngh run list --repo owner/repo --limit 10\n```\n\nView a run and see which steps failed:\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nView logs for failed steps only:\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo --log-failed\n```\n\n## API for Advanced Queries\n\nThe `gh api` command is useful for accessing data not available through other subcommands.\n\nGet PR with specific fields:\n```bash\ngh api repos/owner/repo/pulls/55 --jq '.title, .state, .user.login'\n```\n\n## JSON Output\n\nMost commands support `--json` for structured output.  You can use `--jq` to filter:\n\n```bash\ngh issue list --repo owner/repo --json number,title --jq '.[] | \"\\(.number): \\(.title)\"'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774923090459}}
{"type":"message","id":"eb218769","parentId":"ecb45ee7","timestamp":"2026-03-31T02:11:47.925Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GitHub skill uses `gh` CLI. But `gh` is not authenticated in this environment (we got \"no git remotes found\"). So I can't use gh CLI to post comments.\n\nI could try to use the GitHub web API directly with curl, but that would require a GitHub token which I don't have access to here.\n\nSince I can't directly post comments without gh auth, let me instead:\n1. Update the OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md with the new issues\n2. Try to spawn aoao as a fresh subagent to handle the bugs\n\nLet me try to use sessions_spawn with runtime=\"subagent\" to create a fresh aoao session that should have the correct delivery context.\n\n\nActually, I'm realizing sessions_spawn with runtime=\"subagent\" requires an agentId, and I don't think aoao is a registered subagent. Let me check the AGENTS.md file to understand the session structure better. The real issue is that xixi sends messages to main using sessions_send with the webchat channel in the delivery context, which might be causing the routing problem.\n\nLooking at the session configuration, both the main direct session and xixi's session show webchat as the delivery channel, yet the Feishu messages are still getting through—this suggests the routing might actually be working through the Feishu plugin despite what the delivery context indicates. The aoao agent might be facing a similar routing mismatch that's preventing messages from reaching it.\n\nI could try bypassing the session routing entirely and send the message directly to aoao using the message tool instead.","thinkingSignature":"4fe6a2d8c79c3d45f92f4c097e83b81478febe7edf6af0a6262d9f8616be7d39"},{"type":"text","text":"gh CLI 未认证，无法直接发 comment。改用 message 工具直接发给 aoao，同时更新项目文件。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8s7cd8g36ezv_1","name":"message","arguments":{"action":"send","channel":"feishu","target":"user:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","message":"aoao，现在有两个紧急任务需要你研究：\n\n**任务1（P1）：#58058 - Feishu/Telegram dashboard sync failure**\n- https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/58058\n- 刚开2小时，2026.3.28 regression\n- Feishu/Telegram 与 dashboard 之间实时同步完全破坏\n- 请调研根因，判断是否可提 fix PR\n\n**任务2（P1）：#58041 - Auto-update crash loop**\n- https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/58041\n- 6天内3次夜间宕机，根因已定位\n- auto-update 非原子性导致 config 更新后 binary 仍为旧版\n- 请确认根因，评估是否可提 fix PR\n\n两个任务结果都直接回报给我（main）。"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":64387,"output":590,"cacheRead":21716,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86693,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774923090484,"responseId":"061a6052556be89d9ca5aa235987bbcd"}}
